(861,1755,'Subnormal intellectual functioning which originates during the developmental period. This has multiple potential etiologies, including genetic defects and perinatal insults. Intelligence quotient (IQ) scores are commonly used to determine whether an individual is mentally retarded. IQ scores between 70 and 79 are in the borderline mentally retarded range. Scores below 67 are in the retarded range. (Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p28)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'10231FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(862,1756,'Superficial bacterial infection of the skin.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'133FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(863,1762,'Disease or trauma involving a single peripheral nerve in isolation, or out of proportion to evidence of diffuse peripheral nerve dysfunction. Mononeuropathy multiplex refers to a condition characterized by multiple isolated nerve injuries. Mononeuropathies may result from a wide variety of causes, including ISCHEMIA; traumatic injury; compression; CONNECTIVE TISSUE DISEASES; CUMULATIVE TRAUMA DISORDERS; and other conditions.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'10217FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(864,1763,'A chronic, localized hardening and thickening of the skin. Lesions may be categorized as morphea (guttate, profunda, pansclerotic) or linear (with or without melorheostosis or hemiatrophy). It is twice as common in women as in men. The condition is characterized by skin ischemia, lymphocytic infiltrates, swollen collagen bundles, and thickening of the dermis with reduction of subcutaneous fat.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'10201FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(865,1767,'Physical insults or injuries occurring simultaneously in several parts of the body.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'10142FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(866,1768,'A malignant tumor of plasma cells usually arising in the bone marrow; characterized by diffuse involvement of the skeletal system, hyperglobulinemia, Bence-Jones proteinuria, and anemia.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'10136FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(867,1771,'A progressive condition usually characterized by combined failure of several organs such as the lungs, liver, kidney, along with some clotting mechanisms, usually postinjury or postoperative.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'10132FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(868,1773,'An unknown emergency related to pregnancy or delivery.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:26:45',NULL,NULL,'1507FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
