(1201,2519,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:00',NULL,NULL,'6267FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1202,2524,'A small smooth slightly elevated wart found especially on the face and back of the hands. Occurs chiefly in children and adolescents.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:00',NULL,NULL,'1213FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1203,2527,'A personality disorder marked by a pattern of instability of interpersonal relationships, self-image, and affects, and marked impulsivity beginning by early adulthood and present in a variety of contexts. (DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:01',NULL,NULL,'6246FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1204,2532,'A malignant tumor that has not yet invaded the basement membrane of the epithelial cell of origin and has not spread to other tissues.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:01',NULL,NULL,'6205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1205,2539,'Localized destruction of the tooth surface initiated by decalcification of the enamel followed by enzymatic lysis of organic structures and leading to cavity formation. If left unchecked, the cavity may penetrate the enamel and dentin and reach the pulp. The three most prominent theories used to explain the etiology of the disase are that acids produced by bacteria lead to decalcification; that micro-organisms destroy the enamel protein; or that keratolytic micro-organisms produce chelates that lead to decalcification.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:01',NULL,NULL,'6188FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1206,2541,'Increased intracellular or extracellular fluid in brain tissue. Cytotoxic brain edema (swelling due to increased intracellular fluid) is indicative of a disturbance in cell metabolism, and is commonly associated with hypoxic or ischemic injuries (see HYPOXIA, BRAIN). An increase in extracellular fluid may be caused by increased brain capillary permeability (vasogenic edema), an osmotic gradient, local blockages in interstitial fluid pathways, or by obstruction of CSF flow (e.g., obstructive HYDROCEPHALUS). (From Childs Nerv Syst 1992 Sep; 8(6):301-6)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:01',NULL,NULL,'6174FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
