(1286,2726,'An ocular disease, occurring in many forms, having as its primary characteristics an unstable or a sustained increase in the intraocular pressure which the eye cannot withstand without damage to its structure or impairment of its function. The consequences of the increased pressure may be manifested in a variety of symptoms, depending upon type and severity, such as excavation of the optic disk, hardness of the eyeball, corneal anesthesia, reduced visual acuity, seeing of colored halos around lights, disturbed dark adaptation, visual field defects, and headaches. (Dictionary of Visual Science, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1287,2727,'Swelling of the thyroid gland, mainly due to iodine deficiency','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'16215FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1288,2728,'Acute infectious disease characterized by primary invasion of the urogenital tract. The etiologic agent, NEISSERIA GONORRHOEAE, was isolated by Neisser in 1879.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5176FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1289,2729,'Hereditary metabolic disorder characterized by recurrent acute arthritis, hyperuricemia and deposition of sodium urate in and around the joints, sometimes with formation of uric acid calculi.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5171FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1290,2730,'Disruption of structural continuity of the body as a result of the discharge of firearms.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5162FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1291,2731,'Lateral displacement of the great toe, producing deformity of the first metatarsophalangeal joint with callous, bursa, or bunion formation over the bony prominence.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5149FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1292,2732,'An extremely common benign tumor, occurring most commonly in infancy and childhood, made up of newly formed blood vessels, and resulting from malformation of angioblastic tissue of fetal life. It can occur anywhere in the body but is most frequently noticed in the skin and subcutaneous tissues. About 75% are present at birth, and about 60% occur in the head and neck area. The majority in infancy will regress spontaneously. Some hemangiomas grow rapidly during the early months of life and may be a source of some concern, although virtually all disappear by about 5 years of age. They do not metastasize and simple excision will often be curative. (Dorland, 27th ed; from Stedman, 25th ed; DeVita Jr et al., Cancer: Principles &amp;amp; Practice of Oncology, 3d ed, p1355)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5137FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1293,2733,'Bleeding into the joints. It may arise from trauma or spontaneously in patients with hemophilia.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5135FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1294,2734,'Frank bleeding in the gastrointestinal tract.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5132FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1295,2735,'Severe or complete loss of motor function on one side of the body. This condition is usually caused by BRAIN DISEASES that are localized to the cerebral hemisphere opposite to the side of weakness. Less frequently, BRAIN STEM lesions; cervical SPINAL CORD DISEASES; PERIPHERAL NERVOUS SYSTEM DISEASES; and other conditions may manifest as hemiplegia. The term hemiparesis (see PARESIS) refers to mild to moderate weakness involving one side of the body.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5125FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1296,2736,'A group of inherited disorders characterized by structural alterations within the hemoglobin molecule.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5114FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1297,2737,'A form of anemia in which the bone marrow fails to produce adequate numbers of peripheral blood elements.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5110FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1298,2740,'A self-limited hemorrhagic disorder of the first days of life, caused by a deficiency of the vitamin K-dependent blood coagulation factors II, VII, IX, and X. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5104FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1299,2741,'Severe inability of the liver to function normally, as evidenced by severe jaundice and abnormal levels of ammonia, bilirubin, alkaline phosphatase, glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase, lactic dehydrogenase, and reversal of the albumin/globulin ratio. (Blakiston&amp;amp;#39;s Gould Medical Dictionary, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5099FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1300,2742,'Protrusion of a loop or knuckle of an organ or tissue through an abnormal opening.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5079FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1301,2743,'Abnormal protrusion of the intestine through the abdominal muscles.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1302,2744,'A personality disorder characterized by overly reactive and intensely expressed or overly dramatic behavior, proneness to exaggeration, emotional excitability, and disturbances in interpersonal relationships.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5059FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1303,2745,'A malignant disease characterized by progressive enlargement of the lymph nodes, spleen, and general lymphoid tissue, and the presence of large, usually multinucleate, cells (REED-STERNBERG CELLS) of unknown origin.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5058FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1304,2746,'A circumscribed collection of fluid, especially a collection of fluid in the tunica vaginalis of the testicle or along the spermatic cord. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5047FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1305,2747,'A behavior disorder originating in childhood in which the essential features are signs of developmentally inappropriate inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity. Although most individuals have symptoms of both inattention and hyperactivity-impulsivity, one or the other pattern may be predominant. The disorder is more frequent in males than females. Onset is in childhood. Symptoms often attenuate during late adolescence although a minority experience the full complement of symptoms into mid-adulthood. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5044FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1306,2749,'Disorders characterized by hypersomnolence during normal waking hours that may impair cognitive functioning. Subtypes include primary hypersomnia disorders (e.g., IDIOPATHIC HYPERSOMNOLENCE; NARCOLEPSY; and KLEINE-LEVIN SYNDROME) and secondary hypersomnia disorders where excessive somnolence can be attributed to a known cause (e.g., drug affect, MENTAL DISORDERS, and SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME). (From  J Neurol Sci 1998 Jan 8;153(2):192-202; Thorpy, Principles and Practice of Sleep Medicine, 2nd ed, p320)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5014FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1307,2750,'Persistently high arterial blood pressure. Currently accepted threshold levels are 140 mm Hg systolic and 90 mm Hg diastolic pressure.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5012FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1308,2751,'Hypertrophy or enlargement of the heart.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'5005FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1309,2752,'The condition that results from excessive loss of body water.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'4978FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1310,2753,'Thrombocytopenia occurring in the absence of toxic exposure or a disease associated with decreased platelets. It is mediated by immune mechanisms, in most cases IgG autoantibodies which attach to platelets and subsequently undergo destruction by macrophages. The disease is seen in acute (affecting children) and chronic (adult) forms.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'4968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1311,2754,'Abortion in which not all the products of conception have been expelled.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'4949FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1312,2755,'Failure of voluntary control of the anal sphincters, with involuntary passage of feces and flatus.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'4948FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1313,2757,'Infections in birds and mammals produced by various species of Trichomonas.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'4929FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1314,2758,'Inflammation of the uterine cervix.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:05',NULL,NULL,'17322FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1315,2759,'Inflammation of the liver and liver disease involving degenerative or necrotic alterations of hepatocytes.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4889FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1316,2760,'Inflammation of the endometrium. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4887FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1317,2763,'Inflammation of the joint space(s).','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4881FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1318,2764,'Abnormal protrusion of the intestine into the inguinal canal.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4877FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1319,2768,'Dysfunction of one or more cranial nerves causally related to a traumatic injury. Penetrating and nonpenetrating CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; NECK INJURIES; and trauma to the facial region are conditions associated with cranial nerve injuries.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4873FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1320,2772,'This concept includes injury of liver or gallbladder','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'17101FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1321,2779,'Bleeding into a cerebral hemisphere of the brain, including lobar, subcortical white matter, and basal ganglia hemorrhages. Commonly associated conditions include HYPERTENSION; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOSCLEROSIS; INTRACRANIAL ANEURYSM; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATIONS; CEREBRAL AMYLOID ANGIOPATHY; and CEREBRAL INFARCTION.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4828FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1322,2781,'Uterine bleeding, usually irregular or acyclic, between periods.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4805FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1323,2784,'Injuries to tissues caused by contact with heat, steam, chemicals (BURNS, CHEMICAL), electricity (BURNS, ELECTRIC), or the like.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1324,2785,'Symmetrical osteitis of the four limbs, chiefly localized to the phalanges and the terminal epiphyses of the long bones of the forearm and leg, sometimes extending to the proximal ends of the limbs and the flat bones, and accompanied by dorsal kyphosis and joint involvement. It is often secondary to chronic conditions of the lungs and heart. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4757FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1325,2786,'Calculi occurring in the kidney. Calculi too large to pass spontaneously range in size from 1 cm to the staghorn stones that occupy the renal pelvis and calyces.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4753FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1326,2787,'Abnormally increased convexity in the curvature of the thoracic spine as viewed from the side. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4743FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1327,2788,'Disturbances in sexual desire and the psychophysiologic changes that characterize the sexual response cycle and cause marked distress and interpersonal difficulty. (APA, DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4737FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1328,2789,'Increase in the mass of bone per unit volume.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4730FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1329,2794,'A syndrome characterized by persistent or recurrent fatigue, diffuse musculoskeletal pain, sleep disturbances, and subjective cognitive impairment of 6 months duration or longer. Symptoms are not caused by ongoing exertion; are not relieved by rest; and result in a substantial reduction of previous levels of occupational, educational, social, or personal activities. Minor alterations of immune, neuroendocrine, and autonomic function may be associated with this syndrome. There is also considerable overlap between this condition and FIBROMYALGIA. (From Semin Neurol 1998;18(2):237-42; Ann Intern Med 1994 Dec 15;121(12): 953-9)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4710FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1330,2795,'A chronic, atrophic skin disease characterized by white, angular, flat, well-defined, indurated papules with an erythematous halo and follicular, black, keratotic plugs. It is the most common cause of kraurosis vulvae in females and balanitis xerotica obliterans in males. It is called also white spot disease and Csillag&#39;s disease. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4702FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1331,2797,'Fibrous, bony, cartilaginous and osteocartilaginous fragments in a synovial joint. Major causes are osteochondritis dissecans, synovial chondromatosis, osteophytes, fractured articular surfaces and damaged menisci.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1332,2798,'The anterior concavity in the curvature of the lumbar and cervical spine as viewed from the side. The term usually refers to abnormally increased curvature (hollow back, saddle back, swayback). It does not include lordosis as normal mating posture in certain animals ( = POSTURE + SEX BEHAVIOR, ANIMAL).','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4681FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1333,2800,'Leukemia associated with hyperplasia and overactivity of the lymphoid tissue. There are increased numbers of circulating malignant lymphocytes and lymphoblasts. (Dorland, 28th ed, p919)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4660FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1334,2802,'A protozoan disease caused by four species of the genus PLASMODIUM (P. falciparum (MALARIA, FALCIPARUM), P. vivax (MALARIA, VIVAX), P. ovale, and P. malariae) and transmitted by the bite of an infected female mosquito of the genus Anopheles. Malaria is endemic in parts of Asia, Africa, Central and South America, Oceania, and certain Caribbean islands. It is characterized by extreme exhaustion associated with paroxysms of high fever, sweating, shaking chills, and anemia.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4638FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1335,2804,'A malignant neoplasm derived from cells that are capable of forming melanin, which may occur in the skin of any part of the body, in the eye, or, rarely, in the mucous membranes of the genitalia, anus, oral cavity, or other sites. It occurs mostly in adults and may originate de novo or from a pigmented nevus or malignant lentigo. Melanomas frequently metastasize widely, and the regional lymph nodes, liver, lungs, and brain are likely to be involved. The incidence of malignant skin melanomas is rising rapidly in all parts of the world. (Stedman, 25th ed; from Rook et al., Textbook of Dermatology, 4th ed, p2445)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4605FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1336,2805,'A primary or metastatic malignant neoplasm involving the uterine corpus.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4602FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1337,2806,'Tumors or cancer of the endocrine glands in general or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:06',NULL,NULL,'4600FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1338,2807,'Tumors or cancer of the pancreas.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4581FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1339,2808,'Tumors or cancer of the STOMACH.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4576FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1340,2810,'Cancer of the gums.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4561FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1341,2811,'Tumors or cancer of the LIP.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4558FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1342,2812,'Tumors or cancer of the SALIVARY GLANDS.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4551FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1343,2813,'Cancer or tumors of the bladder.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4532FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1344,2814,'Such malposition and contact of the maxillary and mandibular teeth as to interfere with the highest efficiency during the excursive movements of the jaw that are essential for mastication. (Jablonski, Illustrated Dictionary of Dentistry, 1982)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4528FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1345,2817,'A highly contagious infectious disease caused by MORBILLIVIRUS, common among children but also seen in the nonimmune of any age, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and multiplies in the epithelial cells, spreading throughout the reticuloendothelial system. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4517FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1346,2819,'Syndrome caused by sucking of thick meconium into the lungs, usually by term or post-term infants (often small for gestational age) either in utero or with first breath. The resultant small airway obstruction may produce respiratory distress, tachypnea, cyanosis, pneumothorax, and/or pneumomediastinum.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4514FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1347,2823,'Disturbances in registering an impression, in the retention of an acquired impression, or in the recall of an impression. Memory impairments are associated with DEMENTIA; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; ENCEPHALITIS; ALCOHOLISM (see also ALCOHOL AMNESTIC DISORDER); SCHIZOPHRENIA; and other conditions.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4504FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1348,2827,'Subnormal intellectual functioning which originates during the developmental period. This has multiple potential etiologies, including genetic defects and perinatal insults. Intelligence quotient (IQ) scores are commonly used to determine whether an individual is mentally retarded. IQ scores between 70 and 79 are in the borderline mentally retarded range. Scores below 67 are in the retarded range. (Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p28)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4487FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1349,2828,'Generic term for diseases caused by an abnormal metabolic process. It can be congenital due to inherited enzyme abnormality (METABOLISM, INBORN ERRORS) or acquired due to disease of an endocrine organ or failure of a metabolically important organ such as the liver. (Stedman, 26th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1350,2831,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4467FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1351,2832,'Abnormal protrusion of one or both of the leaflets of the mitral valve into the left atrium during systole. This may be accompanied by mitral regurgitation, systolic murmur, nonejection click, or cardiac arrhythmia.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4448FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1352,2836,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4445FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1353,2839,'Fractures in which the break in bone is not accompanied by an external wound.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4385FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1354,2843,'Form of leukemia characterized by an uncontrolled proliferation of the myeloid lineage and their precursors in the bone marrow and other sites.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1355,2845,'Gross necrosis of the myocardium, as a result of interruption of the blood supply to the area. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1356,2847,'Inflammation of the muscular walls of the heart. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:07',NULL,NULL,'4324FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1357,2848,'A major deviation from normal patterns of behavior.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4312FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1358,2849,'A condition characterized by recurrent episodes of daytime somnolence and lapses in consciousness (microsomnias) that may be associated with automatic behaviors and AMNESIA. CATAPLEXY; SLEEP PARALYSIS, and hypnagogic HALLUCINATIONS frequently accompany narcolepsy. The pathophysiology of this disorder includes sleep-onset rapid eye movement (REM) sleep, which normally follows stage III or IV sleep. (From Neurology 1998 Feb;50(2 Suppl 1):S2-S7)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4310FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1359,2850,'Focal accumulations of edema fluid in the nasal mucosa accompanied by hyperplasia of the associated submucosal connective tissue. Polyps may be neoplasms, foci of inflammation, degenerative lesions, or malformations.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4306FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1360,2852,'A transient unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia that occurs between the second and fifth days of life because the hepatic enzyme GLUCURONOSYLTRANSFERASE required for BILIRUBIN detoxification is inadquedate.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4296FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1361,2856,'Neoplasms of the intracranial components of the central nervous system, including the cerebral hemispheres, basal ganglia, hypothalamus, thalamus, brain stem, and cerebellum. Brain neoplasms are subdivided into primary (originating from brain tissue) and secondary (i.e., metastatic) forms. Primary neoplasms are subdivided into benign and malignant forms. In general, brain tumors may also be classified by age of onset, histologic type, or presenting location in the brain.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4292FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1362,2858,'Clinical association of heavy proteinuria, hypoalbuminemia, and generalized edema.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4268FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1363,2862,'A general term indicating inflammation of a peripheral or cranial nerve. Clinical manifestation may include PAIN; PARESTHESIAS; PARESIS; or HYPESTHESIA.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4259FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1364,2863,'Diseases of the peripheral nerves external to the brain and spinal cord, which includes diseases of the nerve roots, ganglia, plexi, autonomic nerves, sensory nerves, and motor nerves.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4246FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1365,2865,'Failure or imperfection of vision at night or in dim light, with good vision only on bright days. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4240FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1366,2866,'Involuntary discharge of urine after the age at which urinary control should have been achieved; often used alone with specific reference to involuntary discharge of urine occurring during sleep at night (bed-wetting; nocturnal enuresis). (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4239FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1367,2867,'Patient or client refusal of or resistance to medical, psychological, or psychiatric treatment. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4221FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1368,2873,'An enlarged thyroid gland containing circumscribed nodules within its substance. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4208FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1369,2874,'Hemorrhage into the peritoneal cavity.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4207FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1370,2875,'Union of the fragments of a fractured bone in a faulty or abnormal position. If two bones parallel to one another unite by osseous tissue, the result is a crossunion. (From Manual of Orthopaedic Terminology, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4206FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1371,2876,'A fracture in which union fails to occur, the ends of the bone becoming rounded and eburnated, and a false joint occurs. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1372,2880,'Involuntary movements of the eye that are divided into two types, jerk and pendular. Jerk nystagmus has a slow phase in one direction followed by a corrective fast phase in the opposite direction, and is usually caused by central or peripheral vestibular dysfunction. Pendular nystagmus features oscillations that are of equal velocity in both directions and this condition is often associated with visual loss early in life. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p272)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4196FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1373,2881,'Increase in body weight beyond skeletal and physical standards as the result of an excessive accumulation of fat in the body. More than two times the ideal weight is considered OBESITY, MORBID.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4194FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1374,2882,'Abnormally infrequent menstruation.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4172FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1375,2888,'Fractures of the femur.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4165FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1376,2891,'diarrheal illness, usually due to infection','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'151FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1377,2895,'Pathologic process consisting of a partial or complete disruption of the layers of a surgical wound.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4093FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1378,2896,'Disorders related or resulting from abuse or mis-use of opioids.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4090FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1379,2898,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1380,2899,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:08',NULL,NULL,'4077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1381,2900,'A progressive, degenerative joint disease, the most common form of arthritis, especially in older persons. The disease is thought to result not from the aging process but from biochemical changes and biomechanical stresses affecting articular cartilage. In the foreign literature it is often called osteoarthrosis deformans.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'4067FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1382,2908,'A genus of parasitic nematodes whose organisms are distributed in Central and South America. Characteristics include a smooth cuticle and an enlarged anterior end.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'4027FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1383,2910,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'4020FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1384,2912,'Movements or behaviors associated with sleep, sleep stages, or partial arousals from sleep that may impair sleep maintenance. Parasomnias are generally divided into four groups: arousal disorders, sleep-wake transition disorders, parasomnias of REM sleep, and nonspecific parasomnias. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p191)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3998FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1385,2913,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or \"seizure disorder.\"','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3987FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1386,2914,'Fractures occurring as a result of disease of a bone or from some undiscoverable cause, and not due to trauma. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3985FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1387,2918,'Abnormal enlargement or overgrowth of the gingivae brought about by enlargement of existing cells.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1388,2921,'Conditions in which increased pressure within a limited space compromises the circulation and function of tissue within that space. Compartmentation involves mainly the leg but also involved are the forearm, arm, thigh, shoulder, and buttock. Some of the causes of increased pressure are trauma, tight dressings, hemorrhage, and exercise. Sequelae include nerve compression, paralysis, and contracture.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3959FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
