(1390,2923,'Inflammation of the lining of the abdomen and pelvis.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3953FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1391,2924,'A major deviation from normal patterns of behavior.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3950FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1392,2928,'Inflammation of a vein associated with thrombus formation.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3941FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1393,2929,'Psychiatric illness or diseases manifested by breakdowns in the adaptational process expressed primarily as abnormalities of thought, feeling, and behavior producing either distress or impairment of function.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'15797FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1394,2930,'Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3937FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1395,2938,'A placenta which develops in the lower uterine segment, in the zone of dilatation, so that it covers or adjoins the internal os. Painless hemorrhage in the last trimester, particularly during the eighth month, is the most common symptom. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3920FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1396,2939,'A condition or physical state produced by the ingestion, injection or inhalation of, or exposure to a deleterious agent.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3907FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1397,2941,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'15717FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1398,2942,'Infection occurring at the site of a surgical incision.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3865FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1399,2945,'Anxiety disorders manifested by the development of characteristic symptoms following a psychologically traumatic event that is outside the normal range of usual human experience. Symptoms include re-experiencing the traumatic event and numbing of responsiveness to or reduced involvement with the external world.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:09',NULL,NULL,'3854FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1400,2949,'Onset of labor before term but after the fetus has become viable, usually sometime during the 29th through 38th week of gestation.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3846FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
