(1402,2952,'Hereditary metabolic disorder characterized by recurrent acute arthritis, hyperuricemia and deposition of sodium urate in and around the joints, sometimes with formation of uric acid calculi.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3823FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1403,2955,'Tumors or cancer of the biliary tract.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3818FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1404,2956,'Neoplasms of the intracranial components of the central nervous system, including the cerebral hemispheres, basal ganglia, hypothalamus, thalamus, brain stem, and cerebellum. Brain neoplasms are subdivided into primary (originating from brain tissue) and secondary (i.e., metastatic) forms. Primary neoplasms are subdivided into benign and malignant forms. In general, brain tumors may also be classified by age of onset, histologic type, or presenting location in the brain.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3816FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1405,2958,'Tumors or cancer of the EYE.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3813FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1406,2959,'Tumors or cancer of the breast.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3811FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1407,2960,'Tumors or cancers of the KIDNEY.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3802FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1408,2962,'Tumors or cancer of the INTESTINES.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3779FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1409,2963,'Tumors or cancer of the TONGUE.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1410,2965,'The primary sore of syphilis, a painless indurated, eroded papule, occurring at the site of entry of the infection.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3761FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1411,2966,'Subnormal intellectual functioning which originates during the developmental period. This has multiple potential etiologies, including genetic defects and perinatal insults. Intelligence quotient (IQ) scores are commonly used to determine whether an individual is mentally retarded. IQ scores between 70 and 79 are in the borderline mentally retarded range. Scores below 67 are in the retarded range. (Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p28)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3740FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1412,2972,'Embolism in the pulmonary artery or one of its branches.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3688FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1413,2973,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3678FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1414,2974,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1415,2975,'Purplish or brownish red discoloration, easily visible through the epidermis, caused by hemorrhage into the tissues.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3669FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1416,2977,'A cutaneous inflammatory reaction occurring as a result of exposure to ionizing radiation.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3661FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1417,2979,'Condition characterized by splenomegaly, some reduction in the number of circulating blood cells in the presence of a normal or hyperactive bone marrow, and the potential for reversal by splenectomy.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3652FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1418,2983,'The inability of a kidney to excrete metabolites at normal plasma levels under conditions of normal loading, or the inability to retain electrolytes under conditions of normal intake. In the acute form (KIDNEY FAILURE, ACUTE), it is marked by uremia and usually by oliguria or anuria, with hyperkalemia and pulmonary edema. The chronic form (KIDNEY FAILURE, CHRONIC) is irreversible and requires hemodialysis.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1419,2984,'A childhood seizure disorder characterized by rhythmic electrical brain discharges of geneneralized onset. Clinical features include a sudden cessation of ongoing activity usually without loss of postural tone. Rhythmic blinking of the eyelids or lip smacking frequently accompanies the seizure. The usual duration is 5-10 seconds, and multiple episodes may occur daily. Juvenile absence epilepsy is characterized by the juvenile onset of absence seizures and an increased incidence of myoclonus and tonic-clonic seizures. (Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, p736)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'15623FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1420,2985,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3628FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1421,2991,'An acute, usually benign, infectious disease caused by the RUBELLA VIRUS and most often affecting children and nonimmune young adults, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and spreads to the lymphatic system. (From Dorland, 27th edition)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'3592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1422,2992,'Sudden calamitous events producing great material damage, loss, and distress. They are the result of natural phenomena such as earthquakes, floods, etc.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:10',NULL,NULL,'15611FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1423,2996,'Disorders in which there is a loss of ego boundaries or a gross impairment in reality testing with delusions or prominent hallucinations. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3566FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1424,2997,'A personality disorder in which there are oddities of thought (magical thinking, paranoid ideation, suspiciousness), perception (illusions, depersonalization), speech (digressive, vague, overelaborate), and behavior (inappropriate affect in social interactions, frequently social isolation) that are not severe enough to characterize schizophrenia.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3564FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1425,2998,'A chronic, progressive dermatosis characterized by boardlike hardening and immobility of the affected skin, with visceral involvement, especially of lungs, esophagus, kidneys and heart. It may be accompanied by calcinosis, Raynaud&#39;s phenomenon, and telangiectasis (CREST syndrome). It includes acrosclerosis and sclerodactyly.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3557FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1426,2999,'Inflammation of the mucous membrane of the nose similar to that found in hay fever except that symptoms persist throughout the year. The causes are usually air-borne allergens, particularly dusts, feathers, molds, animal fur, etc.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3552FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1427,3000,'A chronic inflammatory disease of the skin of unknown etiology. It is characterized by moderate erythema, dry, moist, or greasy scaling, and yellow crusted patches on various areas, especially the scalp. On the scalp, it generally appears first as small patches of scales, progressing to involve the entire scalp with exfoliation of excessive amounts of dry scales (dandruff).','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3550FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1428,3002,'A general term referring to sudden and often violent motor activity of cerebral or brainstem origin. Convulsions may also occur in the absence of an electrical cerebral discharge (e.g., in response to hypotension).','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3527FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1429,3003,'Systemic disease associated with the presence and persistence of pathogenic microorganisms or their toxins in the blood. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3517FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1430,3005,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3513FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1431,3006,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3509FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1432,3007,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3507FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1433,3009,'A skin condition characterized by the development of recurring boils.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'112FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1434,3010,'A pathological condition that can suddenly affect the hemodynamic equilibrium, usually manifested by failure to perfuse or oxygenate vital organs.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3499FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1435,3011,'Difficult childbirth or labor.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3497FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1436,3012,'A transient loss of consciousness and postural tone caused by diminished blood flow to the brain (i.e., BRAIN ISCHEMIA). Presyncope refers to the sensation of lightheadedness and loss of strength that precedes a syncopal event or accompanies an incomplete syncope. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp367-9)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1437,3013,'Conditions characterized by disturbances of usual sleep patterns or behaviors. Sleep disorders may be divided into three major categories: DYSSOMNIAS (i.e. disorders characterized by insomnia or hypersomnia), PARASOMNIAS (abnormal sleep behaviors), and sleep disorders secondary to medical or psychiatric disorders. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p187)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3474FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1438,3015,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'15592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1439,3019,'A cognitive disorder characterized by an impaired ability to comprehend written and printed words or phrases despite intact vision. This condition may be developmental or acquired. Developmental dyslexia is marked by reading achievement that falls substantially below that expected given the individual&#39;s chronological age, measured intelligence, and age-appropriate education. The disturbance in reading significantly interferes with academic achievement or with activities of daily living that require reading skills. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1440,3022,'A type of acneiform disorder in which secondary pyogenic infection in and around pilosebaceous structures ends in keloidal scarring. It manifests as persistent folliculitis of the back of the neck associated with occlusion of the follicular orifices. It is most often encountered in black or Asian men.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'15583FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1441,3023,'A chronic disorder of the pilosebaceous apparatus associated with an increase in sebum secretion. It is characterized by open comedones (blackheads), closed comedones (whiteheads), and pustular nodules. The cause is unknown, but heredity and age are predisposing factors.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'15578FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1442,3025,'Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3430FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1443,3028,'A collective term for muscle and ligament injuries without dislocation or fracture. A sprain is a joint injury in which some of the fibers of a supporting ligament are ruptured but the continuity of the ligament remains intact. A strain is an overstretching or overexertion of some part of the musculature.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3426FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1444,3030,'A disease of infants due to group 2 phage type 17 staphylococci that produce an epidermolytic exotoxin. Superficial fine vesicles and bullae form and rupture easily, resulting in loss of large sheets of epidermis.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3417FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1445,3032,'Skin diseases characterized by local or general distributions of blisters. They are classified according to the site and mode of blister formation. Lesions can appear spontaneously or be precipitated by infection, trauma, or sunlight. Etiologies include immunologic and genetic factors. (From Scientific American Medicine, 1990)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3378FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1446,3034,'Disorders related to substance abuse, the side effects of a medication, toxin exposure, and alcohol related disorders','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'3374FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1447,3036,'General or unspecified injuries involving the fingers.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:11',NULL,NULL,'15538FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1448,3039,'Clinical syndrome characterized by abdominal pain of great severity associated with other symptoms and signs, usually those of acute peritonitis, which might well be the result of a ruptured abdominal viscus or a similar abdominal catastrophe requiring urgent surgical operation.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15521FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1449,3042,'A chronic, relapsing, inflammatory, and often febrile multisystemic disorder of connective tissue, characterized principally by involvement of the skin, joints, kidneys, and serosal membranes. It is of unknown etiology, but is thought to represent a failure of the regulatory mechanisms of the autoimmune system. The disease is marked by a wide range of system dysfunctions, an elevated erythrocyte sedimentation rate, and the formation of LE cells in the blood or bone marrow.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3347FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1450,3046,'Acute inflammation of the vermiform appendix.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15511FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1451,3047,'A variety of conditions affecting the anatomic and functional characteristics of the temporomandibular joint. Factors contributing to the complexity of temporomandibular diseases are its relation to dentition and mastication and the symptomatic effects in other areas which account for referred pain to the joint and the difficulties in applying traditional diagnostic procedures to temporomandibular joint pathology where tissue is rarely obtained and x-rays are often inadequate or nonspecific. Common diseases are developmental abnormalities, trauma, subluxation, luxation, arthritis, and neoplasia. (From Thoma&#39;s Oral Pathology, 6th ed, pp577-600)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3339FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1452,3048,'Inflammation of the bronchioles. Including acute bronchiolitis due to respiratory syncitial virus, human metapneumovirus, other specified organisms or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15502FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1453,3049,'Downward displacement of the uterus. It is classified in various degrees: in the first degree the cervix is within the vaginal orifice; in the second degree the cervix is outside the orifice; in the third degree the entire uterus is outside the orifice.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3331FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1454,3050,'The presence of abnormal uterine bleeding immediately after labor or childbirth.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3330FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1455,3051,'Condition of vaginal bleeding with or without pain in early pregnancy which may presage an abortion.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1456,3052,'Disorders in which the symptoms are distressing to the individual and recognized by him or her as being unacceptable. Social relationships may be greatly affected but usually remain within acceptable limits. The disturbance is relatively enduring or recurrent without treatment.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3328FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1457,3053,'A decrease in the number of blood platelets.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1458,3054,'Inflammation of the thyroid gland.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3317FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1459,3055,'DEF: Frequent and loose bowel movements of acute onset (&amp;lt; 24 hours).  DESC: Commonly associated with abdominal pain. May be associated with blood or mucus in the stool. REF: http://www.healthatoz.com/healthatoz/Atoz/common/standard/transform.jsp?requestURI=/healthatoz/Atoz/ency/diarrhea.jsp','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15491FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1460,3056,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or seizure disorder','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3302FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1461,3057,'A focal dystonia characterized by a sustained spasmodic contraction of neck muscles. The trapezius and sternocleidomastoid muscles are primarily involved, resulting in twisting of the neck and an unnatural position of the head. Torticollis may occur as a primary disease process or in association with another condition (e.g., NECK INJURIES, the use of ANTIPSYCHOTIC AGENTS, etc.). (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p107)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3297FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1462,3058,'ToxÃ©mie GravÃ©dique','fr',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3295FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1463,3058,'Pregnancy-induced hypertensive states, including EPH gestosis when edema and proteinuria accompany hypertension. Other hypertensive disorders that develop during pregnancy or the puerperium are pre-eclampsia and eclampsia, either of which may be superimposed upon chronic hypertensive vascular or renal disease.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3294FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1465,3060,'Inflammation of the lining of the stomach and intestines, often accompanied by diarrhea.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15476FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1467,3063,'A microscopically inflammatory, usually reversible, patchy hair loss occurring in sharply defined areas and usually involving the beard or scalp. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3271FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1469,3066,'General or unspecified injuries involving the foot.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3268FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1470,3067,'Compulsion to pull out one&amp;#39;s hair.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3261FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1471,3069,'A subgroup of PARAPSORIASIS itself divided into acute and chronic forms. The acute form is characterized by the abrupt onset of a generalized, reddish-brown, maculopapular eruption. Lesions may be vesicular, hemorrhagic, crusted, or necrotic. Histologically the disease is characterized by epidermal necrolysis. The chronic form shows milder skin changes with necrosis. An important variant of the chronic form is LYMPHOMATOID PAPULOSIS.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15451FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1472,3070,'Mycobacterial infection of the bone','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'16793FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1473,3071,'Inflammation of the tonsils of varying degrees of severity and involving simple inflammation.  Associated with acute pharyngitis, streptococcus infection, or formation of an abscess (as quinsy).','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'111FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1474,3073,'Infection of the lymph nodes by tuberculosis. Tuberculous infection of the cervical lymph nodes is scrofula.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3100FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1475,3077,'Inflammation of the middle ear.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'15396FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1476,3078,'Ulceration of the skin and underlying structures of the lower extremity. About 90% of the cases are due to venous insufficiency (VARICOSE ULCER), 5% to arterial disease, and the remaining 5% to other causes.','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:12',NULL,NULL,'3016FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1477,3079,'A loss of mucous substance of the mouth showing local excavation of the surface, resulting from the sloughing of inflammatory necrotic tissue. It is the result of a variety of causes, e.g., denture irritation, aphthous stomatitis (STOMATITIS, APHTHOUS), NOMA, necrotizing gingivitis (GINGIVITIS, NECROTIZING, ULCERATIVE), TOOTHBRUSHING, and various irritants. (From Jablonski, Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p842)','en',2,'2026-03-05 23:27:13',NULL,NULL,'3012FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
